WEBVTT

00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:04.960
Every year we set out to make it our

00:00:02.240 --> 00:00:06.960
best year yet, but before long the

00:00:04.960 --> 00:00:08.960
resolutions fade, the goals get

00:00:06.960 --> 00:00:10.160
dismissed, [music] and we fall back to

00:00:08.960 --> 00:00:12.320
the same old habits.

00:00:10.160 --> 00:00:14.400
>> It really does come down to this concept

00:00:12.320 --> 00:00:16.320
of that's called be do have.

00:00:14.400 --> 00:00:17.760
>> That's Tom Sylvester, a serial

00:00:16.320 --> 00:00:19.840
entrepreneur and business coach [music]

00:00:17.760 --> 00:00:22.240
and someone I personally look to for

00:00:19.840 --> 00:00:24.080
guidance, not just on goal planning, but

00:00:22.240 --> 00:00:28.240
on actually following through on those

00:00:24.080 --> 00:00:30.000
goals. My favorite question is I like to

00:00:28.240 --> 00:00:31.359
like and this might sound a little weird

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:33.200
but

00:00:31.359 --> 00:00:35.440
>> in this video we'll share the concrete

00:00:33.200 --> 00:00:37.360
exercises you can do to get clear on

00:00:35.440 --> 00:00:38.800
where you want to go this year and how

00:00:37.360 --> 00:00:41.200
to stay on track. The

00:00:38.800 --> 00:00:43.360
>> place that I always like to start is

00:00:41.200 --> 00:00:46.320
where we're at. And really that comes

00:00:43.360 --> 00:00:47.840
down to like where we've been. And so

00:00:46.320 --> 00:00:49.680
one of the things that I really like to

00:00:47.840 --> 00:00:51.760
do with people is like especially when

00:00:49.680 --> 00:00:54.320
we're talking about goals, I like to

00:00:51.760 --> 00:00:56.239
look at it from a personal perspective

00:00:54.320 --> 00:00:58.000
and then like a business or a career

00:00:56.239 --> 00:01:00.320
perspective. And so if we're looking at

00:00:58.000 --> 00:01:02.320
it from a personal perspective, I like

00:01:00.320 --> 00:01:04.879
to use this concept called the wheel of

00:01:02.320 --> 00:01:07.520
life. And it sounds super fancy. Really

00:01:04.879 --> 00:01:09.600
what it comes down to is identify areas

00:01:07.520 --> 00:01:11.520
that are important for you in your life.

00:01:09.600 --> 00:01:13.520
Maybe it's your marriage, maybe it's

00:01:11.520 --> 00:01:16.000
your health, maybe it's your finances,

00:01:13.520 --> 00:01:18.400
maybe it's your faith. But have a list

00:01:16.000 --> 00:01:21.280
of those. And then I like to ask two

00:01:18.400 --> 00:01:22.799
questions for each of those. One, on a

00:01:21.280 --> 00:01:26.560
scale of 1 to 10, where would you rate

00:01:22.799 --> 00:01:29.600
that today? And then two, what would

00:01:26.560 --> 00:01:31.439
need to be true to get it to a 10? And I

00:01:29.600 --> 00:01:33.680
think if we can start there, it gets us

00:01:31.439 --> 00:01:35.600
grounded into where we're actually at

00:01:33.680 --> 00:01:37.680
today. And then we can have an

00:01:35.600 --> 00:01:39.600
understanding of where some of those

00:01:37.680 --> 00:01:41.119
gaps are to get it to a 10. And that's

00:01:39.600 --> 00:01:43.119
going to be the starting point for any

00:01:41.119 --> 00:01:44.960
goal setting that we're going to do.

00:01:43.119 --> 00:01:48.479
>> Okay. Okay. So, identifying it sounds

00:01:44.960 --> 00:01:50.079
like four or five core pillars or core,

00:01:48.479 --> 00:01:52.479
you know, segments of the pie on this

00:01:50.079 --> 00:01:54.479
wheel of life and then taking stock of

00:01:52.479 --> 00:01:58.320
where I'm at today on a scale from 1 to

00:01:54.479 --> 00:02:00.159
10. How how am I doing fitness-wise? How

00:01:58.320 --> 00:02:02.399
am I doing relationships wise? How am I

00:02:00.159 --> 00:02:05.119
doing financially? And kind of filling

00:02:02.399 --> 00:02:06.320
in the the current state of affairs on

00:02:05.119 --> 00:02:08.399
the pie.

00:02:06.320 --> 00:02:10.239
>> Exactly. Because here's the thing. If we

00:02:08.399 --> 00:02:11.840
don't know where we're at now, it's

00:02:10.239 --> 00:02:14.160
going to be so hard to figure out where

00:02:11.840 --> 00:02:16.319
we want to go. and we don't know how

00:02:14.160 --> 00:02:17.840
close or far away we are. So, I find

00:02:16.319 --> 00:02:19.599
that if we can just check in on where

00:02:17.840 --> 00:02:21.200
we're at today, that's going to give us

00:02:19.599 --> 00:02:23.120
some clues and some starting point of

00:02:21.200 --> 00:02:24.480
like what should we likely focus on as

00:02:23.120 --> 00:02:27.760
we go forward.

00:02:24.480 --> 00:02:29.680
>> Got it. Got it. Okay. It's similar to

00:02:27.760 --> 00:02:31.760
the the GPS on your phone, right? It's

00:02:29.680 --> 00:02:32.800
like it needs a starting point before it

00:02:31.760 --> 00:02:34.000
could tell you how to get there, what

00:02:32.800 --> 00:02:36.080
turns to take.

00:02:34.000 --> 00:02:37.680
>> Exactly. And now you can go as deep into

00:02:36.080 --> 00:02:39.840
this as you want. So, for example, with

00:02:37.680 --> 00:02:42.000
my wife and I over the years, we I think

00:02:39.840 --> 00:02:43.920
we have like 10 categories and we

00:02:42.000 --> 00:02:46.400
actually spend a decent amount of time

00:02:43.920 --> 00:02:48.959
going into this individually and then we

00:02:46.400 --> 00:02:50.959
come together and we share ours. We

00:02:48.959 --> 00:02:53.120
understand each other's and then

00:02:50.959 --> 00:02:54.879
collectively we can then plan together.

00:02:53.120 --> 00:02:57.280
So, it's like this could be a quick like

00:02:54.879 --> 00:02:59.200
15-inute activity for you or this could

00:02:57.280 --> 00:03:02.000
be a multi-hour activity.

00:02:59.200 --> 00:03:04.560
>> Got it. Got it. Okay. So coming up first

00:03:02.000 --> 00:03:06.080
with these these core areas, the areas

00:03:04.560 --> 00:03:07.920
of your life that are really important

00:03:06.080 --> 00:03:09.360
to you and we named off a few of them.

00:03:07.920 --> 00:03:11.280
It could be health, it could be

00:03:09.360 --> 00:03:13.519
relationships, it could be faith, it

00:03:11.280 --> 00:03:14.879
could be finances, it could you know any

00:03:13.519 --> 00:03:17.920
number of things. It could be community

00:03:14.879 --> 00:03:19.440
service. Whatever it is and then I kind

00:03:17.920 --> 00:03:20.480
of like the idea of comparing notes. I'm

00:03:19.440 --> 00:03:22.480
going to do I'm going to do it on my end

00:03:20.480 --> 00:03:23.707
and then you see it's like oh we're

00:03:22.480 --> 00:03:25.360
we're not on the same page here.

00:03:23.707 --> 00:03:27.680
[laughter] So it could be a good

00:03:25.360 --> 00:03:30.400
conversation. Um, and then do you do the

00:03:27.680 --> 00:03:31.840
same thing business-wise or you know

00:03:30.400 --> 00:03:34.239
kind of having different categories

00:03:31.840 --> 00:03:36.640
because it's like one is one piece of

00:03:34.239 --> 00:03:38.720
the pie to you as an individual but like

00:03:36.640 --> 00:03:39.920
and then on the side hustle or on the

00:03:38.720 --> 00:03:42.720
business side of things it's like well

00:03:39.920 --> 00:03:44.480
that's its own entity. Yep. So I I do

00:03:42.720 --> 00:03:46.799
them separate but I follow a similar

00:03:44.480 --> 00:03:48.319
process. So on the business side we'll

00:03:46.799 --> 00:03:49.920
do the same thing. We'll look at what

00:03:48.319 --> 00:03:51.840
are the categories that are important to

00:03:49.920 --> 00:03:53.680
the business. So for most businesses

00:03:51.840 --> 00:03:55.920
it's like you know how much revenue did

00:03:53.680 --> 00:03:57.439
we make this year? Um, ultimately, how

00:03:55.920 --> 00:03:59.760
much were we able to take home and and

00:03:57.439 --> 00:04:02.720
pay ourselves from that? Um, how was my

00:03:59.760 --> 00:04:04.560
time going? Um, how did my projects go?

00:04:02.720 --> 00:04:07.040
Like the major projects and goals I set

00:04:04.560 --> 00:04:08.080
out, how did I do on them? And then, you

00:04:07.040 --> 00:04:10.799
know, what are some of the biggest

00:04:08.080 --> 00:04:12.400
